{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-22T21:41:30.010Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"003810f1fa9492781312030a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-22T21:41:30.010Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-22T21:41:30.010Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"## Host behavior\n\n- `not ok 32 - native harness exercises all seven commands with equivalent scoped JSON and TOON`. The old harness accepted a package cursor through `outputCursor` and delivered `invalid_input` from the package for conflicting or malformed cursors. The host now validates the native cursor before dispatch and reports `read_output_cursor_invalid` with exit 2. The native assertions check those refusals and still resume via the package `--cursor`. The original package guards run directly with the real SDK.\n- The same test previously saw package `invalid_input` for an array-valued `--tuple` and a malformed output session. The host now refuses these as `extension_flag_value_invalid` and `invalid_read_output_session`. The tests check both host codes and keep the handler-level refusals.\n- `not ok 37 - an explicit budget is not refused by an invalid stored budget setting`. An array-valued `--budget` used to enter the handler and produce a package refusal. The host now rejects arrays for scalar flags before dispatch. The native assertion expects `extension_flag_value_invalid` with exit 2, and the handler assertion retains `invalid_input`. Valid explicit budgets, invalid scalar budgets, stored policy fallback and pre-write reservation remain covered.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Baseline build and typecheck passed. The full baseline passed 114 of 116 tests. Both updated failure classes fail with a missing expected host rejection when run against 2026.11.14 in a disposable checkout.\n- `pm test pm-case-sdk-1122 --run --progress` passed 6 of 6 contract tests.\n- `npm run release:check` and `bun run release:check` each passed 116 of 116 tests. Coverage is 614/614 statements, 355/355 branches, 173/173 functions, and 498/498 lines. The gates include typecheck, lint, identity and privacy, tracker health, changelog, production audit, packed npm and Bun acceptance, and behavioral and linked-build reverts.\n\nCI for this branch is tracked in the Actions run list. [Branch runs](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions?query=branch%3Adeps%2Fadopt-pm-cli-host-alignment-1122)"}]}],"before_hash":"8fced5c6251fa11ebefc06f5354fef463934233746382f62702d28a4fba7c3fe","after_hash":"b04e47533060abca82382335fe95805cb3458c8200ce706632c658b3d6f8c255","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0fa21b7fc6917e0f07d5fea3434ed0abaafc60956a87cc15c26c7cd349fa92e1"}
